-- Discovery diagnostics, one union per table that stores them.
--
-- A diagnostic row stores the union of its own table, so a table cannot hold
-- a code that belongs to another (a lexer table holding "cannot find source
-- file", a root row holding an unknown escape). A variant carries exactly the
-- arguments its code has, typed as what they are: an `ImportId`, a `PathId`,
-- a number. The message is rendered from the value at the boundary that shows
-- it, so the text lives in one place: `diagnostics/render.brp`.
--
-- Tables and their unions:
--
-- - lexer and parser rows (`SyntaxDiagnosticAt`): `SyntaxDiagnostic`
-- - module graph rows (`ResolutionDiagnosticRow`): `ResolutionDiagnostic`
-- - root rows (`RootDiagnosticRow`): `RootDiagnostic`
-- - implicit module rows (`ImplicitDiagnosticRow`): `ImplicitDiagnostic`
--
-- Variant names are module-wide, so the three module graph unions name the
-- limits of the same two rejections apart (`ImportSourceTooLarge`,
-- `RootSourceTooLarge`, `ImplicitSourceTooLarge`); `diagnostic_name` gives
-- all of them one stable spelling, `<Variant>Diagnostic`, for dumps and
-- fixtures.
import:
	expected_token:
		ExpectedTokenDiagnostic(
			ExpectedArrow, ExpectedColon, ExpectedComma, ExpectedEqual, ExpectedFatArrow,
			ExpectedIndent, ExpectedKeyword, ExpectedLeftBrace, ExpectedLeftParen, ExpectedName,
			ExpectedNewline, ExpectedRightBrace, ExpectedRightBracket, ExpectedRightParen,
		),
	ids: DefinitionId, ImportId, LiteralId, NameId, PathId
	span: Span


---
A lexer or parser diagnostic that has no argument:

- `UnterminatedDocstringDiagnostic`: A `---` docstring has no closing `---` line.
- `UnterminatedStringDiagnostic`: A string literal reaches the end of the source.
- `MultilineStringDiagnostic`: A string literal reaches the end of its line.
- `UnterminatedEscapeDiagnostic`: A backslash is the last byte of the source.
- `UnicodeEscapeDigitCountDiagnostic`: A `\u{...}` escape has no digits or more than six.
- `UnicodeEscapeNonHexDiagnostic`: A `\u{...}` escape holds a non-hex character.
- `UnterminatedUnicodeEscapeDiagnostic`: A `\u{...}` escape reaches the end of the source.
- `UnicodeCodepointOutOfRangeDiagnostic`: A `\u{...}` escape names a surrogate or a value above U+10FFFF.
- `MultilineRawStringDiagnostic`: A raw string literal reaches the end of its line.
- `UnterminatedRawStringDiagnostic`: A raw string literal reaches the end of the source.
- `InterpolatedEscapeAtEndDiagnostic`: An interpolated string ends in a backslash at the end of the source.
- `MultilineInterpolatedStringDiagnostic`: An interpolated string reaches the end of its line.
- `UnterminatedInterpolatedStringDiagnostic`: An interpolated string reaches the end of the source.
- `InvalidCharLiteralDiagnostic`: A character literal does not hold exactly one character.
- `UnterminatedCharLiteralDiagnostic`: A character literal reaches the end of the source.
- `UnexpectedCharacterDiagnostic`: A character starts no token; the span covers it.
- `InconsistentIndentationDiagnostic`: A dedent returns to no enclosing indentation level.
- `ExpectedColonAfterImportDiagnostic`: `import` is not followed by `:`.
- `ExpectedNewlineAfterImportHeaderDiagnostic`: `import:` is not followed by a new line.
- `ExpectedIndentedImportsDiagnostic`: The import items are not indented under `import:`.
- `ExpectedModulePathDiagnostic`: An import item does not start with a module path, or a `/` is not followed by a path part.
- `ImportPathCurrentNotLeadingDiagnostic`: A `.` segment follows a module name in an import path; `./` may only start a path. The span is the `.`.
- `ImportPathParentNotLeadingDiagnostic`: A `..` segment follows a module name or a `./` prefix in an import path; `../` may only repeat at the start. The span is the `..`.
- `ExpectedImportSymbolDiagnostic`: A selected symbol is not a name.
- `ExpectedCommaBetweenImportSymbolsDiagnostic`: Two selected symbols are not separated by `,`.
- `ExpectedConstructorNameDiagnostic`: A `name(...)` selection lists no constructor, or lists a non-name.
- `ExpectedClosingParenAfterConstructorsDiagnostic`: A `name(...)` selection is not closed by `)`.
- `ExpectedAliasNameDiagnostic`: `as` is not followed by a name, or is followed by a reserved keyword.
- `ExpectedImportSymbolsAfterColonDiagnostic`: The `:` after a module path is followed by neither symbols nor an indented symbol block.
- `ExpectedDimensionDiagnostic`: A dimension (`#N`, `#3`, `#_` or a dimension expression) is required and none is written.
- `ExpectedTypeDiagnostic`: A type is required and none is written.
- `ArrayDimensionsExpectedDiagnostic`: An array suffix `[...]` holds something other than dimensions.
- `TupleArityDiagnostic`: A tuple type or tuple binder has fewer than two or more than four elements.
- `ExpectedEqualEqualDiagnostic`: `==` is required in a dimension constraint.
- `ExpectedHashDiagnostic`: `#` is required before a dimension.
- `AnnotationArgumentsDiagnostic`: A function annotation is written with arguments.
- `AnnotationWithoutFunctionDiagnostic`: Annotations are not followed by a function declaration.
- `DocstringBeforeImportBlockDiagnostic`: A docstring sits directly before an import block that is not the first thing in the module; only the module's leading docstring may precede an import block. The span is the docstring's.
- `ExpectedDeclarationDiagnostic`: A top-level item does not start a declaration.
- `ForeignFunctionOutsideBlockDiagnostic`: `foreign func` is written without a `foreign:` block.
- `ExpectedForeignArgumentDiagnostic`: A foreign block's parentheses hold no argument.
- `ExpectedForeignArgumentValueDiagnostic`: A foreign block argument's value is not a string literal.
- `ExpectedForeignFunctionDiagnostic`: A foreign block holds something other than a function signature.
- `ExpectedForeignCNameDiagnostic`: `=` after a foreign function signature is not followed by a string literal.
- `ExpectedCleanupBuiltinNameDiagnostic`: A resource type's `builtin(...)` does not hold a string literal.
- `BuiltinTypeArgumentsDiagnostic`: A non-resource builtin type declaration is written with arguments.
- `ExpectedSupertraitOrMethodsDiagnostic`: `trait Name:` is followed by neither supertraits nor a method block.
- `ExpectedImplMethodDiagnostic`: An `implements` block holds something other than a method.
- `ExpectedExpressionDiagnostic`: An expression is required here and none is written.
- `ExpectedPatternDiagnostic`: A match pattern is required here and none is written.
- `ExpectedNumberAfterMinusDiagnostic`: `-` in a pattern is not followed by a number literal.
- `ExpectedSpreadTargetDiagnostic`: `...` in a list pattern is followed by neither a name nor `_`.
- `ExpectedAssignmentOperatorDiagnostic`: A typed name in statement position is followed by no `=`, `?=` or compound assignment.
- `DiscardedQuestionBindDiagnostic`: `_ ?= value` binds the unwrapped value to `_`.
- `FieldAssignmentDiagnostic`: `x.field = value` assigns to a field; record update syntax is required.
- `AssignmentInConditionDiagnostic`: An `if` or `while` condition holds `=` after an expression; the span is the `=`.
- `AssignmentInExpressionDiagnostic`: An assignment (`=`, `?=` or a compound `+=`, `-=`, `*=`, `/=`) follows an expression where only a value may be written; the span is the operator.
- `ExpectedBuiltinNameDiagnostic`: `builtin(` is not followed by a string literal name.
- `RemovedTypeAscriptionDiagnostic`: `value as Type` is removed; the span covers `as`, and parsing skips the type.
- `ExpectedConcurrentParameterDiagnostic`: The parentheses after `concurrent` or `concurrently` hold no parameter.
- `ConcurrentForTupleBinderDiagnostic`: `for (a, b) in xs concurrently` has more than one loop variable.
- `ConcurrentForMaxThreadsDiagnostic`: `concurrently(...)` holds `max_threads`, which belongs to `concurrent(...)`.
- `ConcurrentMaxThreadsNotPositiveLiteralDiagnostic`: `max_threads` is not a positive integer literal.
- `ConcurrentLimitNotPositiveLiteralDiagnostic`: `limit` is not a positive integer literal.
- `ConcurrentForMissingLimitDiagnostic`: A non-empty `concurrently(...)` list has no `limit`.
- `SingletonTupleDiagnostic`: A tuple expression has one element, `(x,)`; the span is the parenthesized tuple.
- `ForExpressionDiagnostic`: `for` is written where a value is required (an assignment value, a call argument, an operand); `for` is a statement. The span is the keyword.
- `WithMultipleBindingsDiagnostic`: A `with` header binds more than one resource.
- `InterpolationHoleNotExpressionDiagnostic`: An interpolation hole holds more than one expression.
- `InterpolatedStringPatternDiagnostic`: A string with `${...}` holes is written as a match pattern.
- `QuestionBindInLoopDiagnostic`: `name ?= value` is written inside a `while`, `for` or `for ... concurrently` body; the span is the `?=`.
- `BreakOutsideLoopDiagnostic`: `break` is written outside every loop body, or in a function body nested in one; the span is the keyword.
- `ContinueOutsideLoopDiagnostic`: `continue` is written outside every loop body, or in a function body nested in one; the span is the keyword.
- `InterpolationTooDeepDiagnostic`: Interpolation holes nest more deeply than the lexer allows.
- `UnionVariantTooManyFieldsDiagnostic`: A union variant declares more payload fields than a variant's ownership bitmask has bits for; the span is the variant's name.
- `MissingFunctionBodyDiagnostic`: A local function, implementation method or trait method with a `:` has no body; the span is the function's name.
- `UnpairedForwardDeclarationDiagnostic`: A top-level function has no body and no same-named top-level function supplies one; the span is the function's name.
- `DiscardedCompoundAssignmentDiagnostic`: `_ += value` and its siblings update `_`, which holds no value; the span is the `_`.
- `EnumCaseParenthesesDiagnostic`: An `enum` case is written with parentheses, `Case(T, ...)` or `Case()`; an `enum` case is only a name, and only a `union` case holds values. The span is the case name.
- `BoundInTypeDiagnostic`: A trait bound `Name: Bound` is written inside a type outside an `implements` receiver, such as `x: (T: Bound)` or `List[T: Bound]`; a bound belongs in a declaration's type-parameter list. The span is the name through the last bound.
- `DimensionParameterBoundsDiagnostic`: A dimension parameter (`#N` or `#_`) is written with trait bounds `#N: Bound`; the span is the `:`.
---
enum PlainSyntaxCode:
	UnterminatedDocstringDiagnostic
	UnterminatedStringDiagnostic
	MultilineStringDiagnostic
	UnterminatedEscapeDiagnostic
	UnicodeEscapeDigitCountDiagnostic
	UnicodeEscapeNonHexDiagnostic
	UnterminatedUnicodeEscapeDiagnostic
	UnicodeCodepointOutOfRangeDiagnostic
	MultilineRawStringDiagnostic
	UnterminatedRawStringDiagnostic
	InterpolatedEscapeAtEndDiagnostic
	MultilineInterpolatedStringDiagnostic
	UnterminatedInterpolatedStringDiagnostic
	InvalidCharLiteralDiagnostic
	UnterminatedCharLiteralDiagnostic
	UnexpectedCharacterDiagnostic
	InconsistentIndentationDiagnostic
	ExpectedColonAfterImportDiagnostic
	ExpectedNewlineAfterImportHeaderDiagnostic
	ExpectedIndentedImportsDiagnostic
	ExpectedModulePathDiagnostic
	ImportPathCurrentNotLeadingDiagnostic
	ImportPathParentNotLeadingDiagnostic
	ExpectedImportSymbolDiagnostic
	ExpectedCommaBetweenImportSymbolsDiagnostic
	ExpectedConstructorNameDiagnostic
	ExpectedClosingParenAfterConstructorsDiagnostic
	ExpectedAliasNameDiagnostic
	ExpectedImportSymbolsAfterColonDiagnostic
	ExpectedDimensionDiagnostic
	ExpectedTypeDiagnostic
	ArrayDimensionsExpectedDiagnostic
	TupleArityDiagnostic
	ExpectedEqualEqualDiagnostic
	ExpectedHashDiagnostic
	AnnotationArgumentsDiagnostic
	AnnotationWithoutFunctionDiagnostic
	DocstringBeforeImportBlockDiagnostic
	ExpectedDeclarationDiagnostic
	ForeignFunctionOutsideBlockDiagnostic
	ExpectedForeignArgumentDiagnostic
	ExpectedForeignArgumentValueDiagnostic
	ExpectedForeignFunctionDiagnostic
	ExpectedForeignCNameDiagnostic
	ExpectedCleanupBuiltinNameDiagnostic
	BuiltinTypeArgumentsDiagnostic
	ExpectedSupertraitOrMethodsDiagnostic
	ExpectedImplMethodDiagnostic
	ExpectedExpressionDiagnostic
	ExpectedPatternDiagnostic
	ExpectedNumberAfterMinusDiagnostic
	ExpectedSpreadTargetDiagnostic
	ExpectedAssignmentOperatorDiagnostic
	DiscardedQuestionBindDiagnostic
	FieldAssignmentDiagnostic
	AssignmentInConditionDiagnostic
	AssignmentInExpressionDiagnostic
	ExpectedBuiltinNameDiagnostic
	RemovedTypeAscriptionDiagnostic
	ExpectedConcurrentParameterDiagnostic
	ConcurrentForTupleBinderDiagnostic
	ConcurrentForMaxThreadsDiagnostic
	ConcurrentMaxThreadsNotPositiveLiteralDiagnostic
	ConcurrentLimitNotPositiveLiteralDiagnostic
	ConcurrentForMissingLimitDiagnostic
	SingletonTupleDiagnostic
	ForExpressionDiagnostic
	WithMultipleBindingsDiagnostic
	InterpolationHoleNotExpressionDiagnostic
	InterpolatedStringPatternDiagnostic
	QuestionBindInLoopDiagnostic
	BreakOutsideLoopDiagnostic
	ContinueOutsideLoopDiagnostic
	InterpolationTooDeepDiagnostic
	UnionVariantTooManyFieldsDiagnostic
	MissingFunctionBodyDiagnostic
	UnpairedForwardDeclarationDiagnostic
	DiscardedCompoundAssignmentDiagnostic
	EnumCaseParenthesesDiagnostic
	BoundInTypeDiagnostic
	DimensionParameterBoundsDiagnostic


---
What the lexer or parser reports, with its arguments.

- `Plain`: A diagnostic with no argument (`PlainSyntaxCode`).
- `ExpectedToken`: A required token or layout is missing; carries which and the construct being parsed (`ExpectedTokenDiagnostic`).
- `UnknownEscape`: A backslash escape names no escape. Carries the escaped byte (any byte: the source may not be valid UTF-8).
- `IntegerLiteralOverflow`: An integer literal exceeds the Int128 range. Carries its digits as written.
- `FloatLiteralOverflow`: A float literal is not finite as a `Float`. Carries its digits as written.
- `UnexpectedByte`: A byte starts no token and no UTF-8 character. Carries the byte.
- `ReservedKeywordAsName`: A reserved keyword is written where a name belongs; the span starts at it (it may be empty) and parsing continues as if it were the name. Carries the `NameId` of the keyword's spelling.
- `UnknownAnnotation`: An `@annotation` names no annotation the language defines. Carries the `NameId` of the annotation's name.
- `ConcurrentDuplicateParameter`: A concurrency parameter name appears twice in one parameter list. Carries the `NameId` of the parameter's name.
- `ConcurrentUnknownParameter`: `concurrent(...)` holds a name other than `max_threads` or `timeout`. Carries the `NameId` of the parameter's name.
- `ConcurrentForUnknownParameter`: `concurrently(...)` holds a name other than `limit` or `timeout`. Carries the `NameId` of the parameter's name.
- `DuplicateFieldGiven`: A record literal or record update gives a field name twice; the span is the second name. Carries the `Span` of the first.
- `DuplicateField`: A record declares a field name twice; the span is the second field's name. Carries the `DefinitionId` of the first field of that name.
---
union SyntaxDiagnostic:
	Plain(PlainSyntaxCode)
	ExpectedToken(ExpectedTokenDiagnostic)
	UnknownEscape(Char)
	IntegerLiteralOverflow(String)
	FloatLiteralOverflow(String)
	UnexpectedByte(Char)
	ReservedKeywordAsName(NameId)
	UnknownAnnotation(NameId)
	ConcurrentDuplicateParameter(NameId)
	ConcurrentUnknownParameter(NameId)
	ConcurrentForUnknownParameter(NameId)
	DuplicateField(DefinitionId)
	DuplicateFieldGiven(Span)


---
What the module graph reports against an import that loaded no module.

- `UnresolvedImport`: An import names a module no source provider has. Carries the `ImportId` of the import.
- `ImportCaseMismatch`: An import names a module that exists only under different letter case. Carries the `ImportId` of the import, then the `PathId` of the path below the resolving directory as the source provider stores it (the text to write instead).
- `UnverifiableSpelling`: A source exists but a directory on the way to it could not be listed, so its spelling could not be checked. Carries the `ImportId` of the requesting import.
- `UnreadableSource`: A source the provider located could not be read. Carries the `ImportId` of the requesting import.
- `ImportSourceTooLarge`: A source is too large for its spans to be packed. Carries the source's byte length: the rejected source is never admitted, so no row of the tables holds it.
- `ImportTooManySources`: Discovery reached more sources than a span can number.
---
union ResolutionDiagnostic:
	UnresolvedImport(ImportId)
	ImportCaseMismatch(ImportId, PathId)
	UnverifiableSpelling(ImportId)
	UnreadableSource(ImportId)
	ImportSourceTooLarge(Int)
	ImportTooManySources


---
What the module graph reports against a root request that loaded no module.

- `UnresolvedRoot`: A root request names a module no source provider has.
- `RootCaseMismatch`: A root request names a source that exists only under different letter case. Carries the `PathId` of the file name as the source provider stores it.
- `UnverifiableRootSpelling`: A root request names a source that exists but a directory on the way to it could not be listed, so its spelling could not be checked.
- `UnreadableRootSource`: A source a root request located could not be read.
- `RootSourceTooLarge`: As `ImportSourceTooLarge`, for a root.
- `RootTooManySources`: As `ImportTooManySources`, for a root.
---
union RootDiagnostic:
	UnresolvedRoot
	RootCaseMismatch(PathId)
	UnverifiableRootSpelling
	UnreadableRootSource
	RootSourceTooLarge(Int)
	RootTooManySources


---
What the module graph reports against an implicit module request that loaded no module.

- `MissingImplicitModule`: An implicit module (see `ImplicitModules` in `pipeline`) has no source in the standard library.
- `UnverifiableImplicitSpelling`: An implicit module's source exists but a directory on the way to it could not be listed, so its spelling could not be checked.
- `UnreadableImplicitSource`: A source the provider located for an implicit module could not be read.
- `ImplicitSourceTooLarge`: As `ImportSourceTooLarge`, for an implicit module.
- `ImplicitTooManySources`: As `ImportTooManySources`, for an implicit module.
---
union ImplicitDiagnostic:
	MissingImplicitModule
	UnverifiableImplicitSpelling
	UnreadableImplicitSource
	ImplicitSourceTooLarge(Int)
	ImplicitTooManySources


---
A stable name for each plain code, for dumps and fixtures.
---
